PitBull4 for WoW Forever (TOC Interface 16001) — patch against PitBull4 v4.2.50
================================================================================

Base:    PitBull4 v4.2.50 (References/addon-sources/pitbull-unit-frames-4-0/PitBull4-v4.2.50.zip,
         sha256 f0f5469329ce64dc0178db634366eba77a3a29f1945356444b839f92cb4fb5e4), folder PitBull4.
Result:  Collection/AddOns/PitBull4 (folder name unchanged; version v4.2.50-forever.1).

Source of the Forever changes (external work, attributed here):
  The Lua/XML changes in this patch are ported from the PitBull4 "4.2.49-Forever-v42" build
  (TOC Author line: 핏빛분노; X-Original-Author: ckknight, Shekfi, Nebula), found in
  work/old-reference-r36-3ed3y_p1/extracted-forever-v42/Interface/AddOns/PitBull4/.
  That build's own readme names as its bases PitBull4 v4.2.49, https://github.com/nebularg/PitBull4/pull/104
  and https://github.com/Thrumbar/PitBull4/commit/db932d0a5df75960977f94ba8b23328e23a17652.
  The original PitBull4 authors are ckknight, Shekfi and Nebula.

What the port does (DevilForever choices):
  - every file the Forever build changed is taken from it, except:
      Libs/LibDBIcon-1.0, Libs/LibDualSpec-1.0, Libs/AceGUI-3.0/widgets/AceGUIWidget-Slider.lua
        (v4.2.50 ships newer library versions; LibDualSpec stays unloaded),
      PitBull4_Cata/Mainline/Mists/TBC.toc and load.xml (kept as in v4.2.50);
  - the v4.2.50 SmartRace guard (Modules/LuaTexts/ScriptEnv.lua, "and C_TooltipInfo") is kept;
  - new PitBull4_Camelot.toc and PitBull4.toc (Interface 16001, modules_Camelot.xml), version
    v4.2.50-forever.1; the Forever build's Classic/Vanilla TOCs, modules_Vanilla.xml and readme
    are not included.
  - less repeated work at run time, displayed values unchanged: native aura containers and
    button styles rebuilt only when settings, unit or frame geometry change (Modules/Aura/Forever.lua,
    one update per combat transition); LuaTexts code classification cached and plain GUID
    comparison in the event loop; health/power bars redrawn once per rendered frame, one power
    event, no per-call closures; LiveStatusBar texture set only when it changes; aura entries
    normalised without per-field closures, ownership computed once per entry; alternate mana bar
    on player/vehicle unit events only; Forever cast bar polled only while a shown frame casts.
  - a "targetpet" singleton (Utils.lua unit ids, Main.lua classifications and target-change
    refresh); on Forever the Totems module exists for shamans only (Modules/Totems/Totems.lua).

Line endings: the v4.2.50 files use CRLF, and so do all changed and added files; the hunks below
carry the CR bytes. Apply from the folder that holds PitBull4/:
    patch -p1 --binary < PitBull4.patch
